        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "All three hashes are identical (the only diff was the path prefix in my md5 listing) — the Python implementation matches GnuCOBOL exactly. Original state and INPUT.DAT have been restored.\n\n**Done.** `/app/program.py` re-implements `program.cbl`:\n\n- Reads the 22-byte fixed record from `/app/src/INPUT.DAT` (buyer, seller, book, PIC 9(10) amount; short records space-padded like GnuCOBOL).\n- Validates buyer/seller exist in ACCOUNTS.DAT (34-byte records: ID X(4), name X(20), balance 9(10)) and that BOOKS.DAT contains the book owned by the seller.\n- On success: subtracts amount from buyer's balance, adds to seller's (zero-padded 10 digits), transfers book ownership to the buyer, and appends a 22-byte transaction record (`book + amount + seller + buyer`) to TRANSACTIONS.DAT.\n- Prints the same messages (\"Transaction failed due to validation errors\" / \"Transaction completed successfully\") and leaves files untouched on failure.\n\nVerified against the compiled COBOL program with both a valid transaction input and the given short/invalid input — resulting `.DAT` file checksums are identical.",
